    "narrative": "The primary engine for Ghost Ride the WHIP today is **Corbin Carroll**, who leads our squad with a robust score of 78.71. His matchup against McGreevy (4.43 xERA) provides an ideal environment for his speed-oriented profile, and his move up to the #2 spot in the order maximizes his run-scoring potential. **Vinnie Pasquantino** follows closely with a 69.63 score; despite the lineup pending, his projected placement at #3 against the contact-prone Troy Melton makes him a critical anchor. **Gabriel Moreno** rounds out our high-efficiency tier at 60.09, benefiting from a favorable platoon advantage against a right-handed arm and maintaining a solid xwOBA of 0.374. \n\nWe are navigating a few \"Lineup Pending\" risks today, specifically with **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Zach McKinstry**. While **Zach McKinstry** remains a marginal play at 54.61, the 19% SP skill boost against the vulnerable Randy Dobnak keeps him in the mix as a high-upside gamble. **Austin Riley** (54.41) and **Travis Bazzana** (44.49) represent our lower-floor options; **Travis Bazzana** is particularly vulnerable due to a tough matchup against T. Bradley, though his platoon edge keeps him ahead of the bench. We are currently hoarding speed assets like **Jose Caballero**, **Mickey Moniak**, and **Brice Turang** on the bench, but they were squeezed out today by the superior projected efficiency of our middle-of-the-order bats. With no games scheduled for **Josh Naylor**, **James Wood**, or **Tyler Soderstrom**, the depth of the Ghost Ride the WHIP roster is preserved for the upcoming weekend push, keeping our game cap discipline intact.",
